## v8.10 (October 2026)

**New protocol on tagged OOS v8.8. Tagged `smt_scanner_v8_8.py` is not modified.**

### Changed
- **Dual-confirm SMT** — v8.8 (and v8.7) score an ES-confirm pair first and skip NQ-confirm whenever ES-confirm exists. That drops a valid NQ-confirm / ES-fail SMT on the same sw2 (example: 2026-10-05 NY Morning 09:14 sw1 / 09:24 sw2). v8.10 runs both sides independently. Dedup remains `(date, sw2_conf_time, direction, instrument)`, so ES LONG and NQ LONG at the same sw2 are two identities.
- **sw1 staleness 90 minutes** — confirm-side sw1 may not be older than 90 minutes from confirm-side sw2 (`SW1_STALENESS_MINS = 90`; equal to 90 is allowed). Failed parallels older than that are dropped before primary/alt selection. If none remain, that sw2 is not SMT. Explicit live-review request after 2026-10-06 07:37/09:18 (101 min). Does not change `SW2_STALENESS_MINS_1M` (sw2 vs scan bar). Tagged OOS v8.8 is unchanged.
- SMT_IN_FVG / FVG_AFTER_SMT clocks, exact sw1/sw2 timestamp match, and FVG search from `sw2_conf_idx` are unchanged from tagged OOS v8.8.

Live: `python -m live_scanners.v810` alongside frozen v8.7 and tagged OOS v8.8.

