## v8.9 (September 2026) — NOT RUN LIVE · OMITTED FROM FUTURE VERSIONS

> **Status: v8.9 is not being run live, and its change is deliberately omitted from all future scanner versions.**
> The membership change below is the change that created v8.9, and it is the reason v8.9 is not run live.
> That change has been chosen to be left out going forward. This is why **v8.10 does not include it**: v8.10 is
> built from the tagged OOS v8.8 file (`v8.8` tag), not from v8.9, and keeps v8.8's confirmation-bar-close
> SMT_IN_FVG membership test. `smt_scanner_v8_9.py` stays in the repo as a historical record only.

**SMT_IN_FVG membership: confirming-instrument swing wicks inside a pre-existing FVG.**

### Changed (the omitted change)
- **Membership check** — v8.8 fires SMT_IN_FVG when the confirmation-bar **close** sits inside a pre-existing FVG. v8.9 instead fires when the confirming instrument's **sw1 and/or sw2 wick prices** sit inside that FVG's `[low, high]`. One or both swings is enough. Same lookback, contiguity, pre-session, imbalance, and size guards; only the inside-FVG predicate changed.
- **Close-only setups are excluded** — a candidate whose confirmation close is inside a pre-FVG but neither swing is does **not** fall through to `FVG_AFTER_SMT`.

Unchanged from v8.8: market entry at confirmation-bar close (`sw2_conf_idx + 1`), FVG-boundary SL (1.0pt ES / 3.0pt NQ buffer, 20/40-tick floor) on the pre-FVG the swing sits in, TP 1.5R, 15m/5m at the confirmation clock, no wait for displacement, `FVG_AFTER_SMT` path otherwise identical.

Tests: `test_smt_in_fvg_swing_membership.py`.

